#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:1
msgid "Move a Sphinx project to Guidedog"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:4
msgid "Guidedog follows Sphinx closely. It uses the same directory structure and understands standard reStructuredText and MyST Markdown markup. It recognizes the same configuration setting names and provides Sphinx's Jinja template variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:8
msgid "One difference shapes the whole move. Sphinx runs arbitrary Python code in ``conf.py`` and needs a Python virtual environment with external packages. Guidedog is a single compiled program that reads plain data from ``conf.toml``. It does not run Python."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:13
msgid "So moving a project means separating configuration data from Python code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:16
msgid "Migration workflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:19
msgid "The move goes through these steps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:23
msgid "conf.py is converted by guidedog migrate into conf.toml, followed by semantic verification, custom object mapping, and visual inspection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:23
msgid "The step-by-step workflow for migrating a Sphinx project to Guidedog."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:42
msgid "Step 1: Automated configuration migration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:45
msgid "Guidedog has a migration tool that parses our existing ``conf.py``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:51
msgid "What ``guidedog migrate`` does:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:53
msgid "It extracts literal configuration values (strings, numbers, booleans, lists, and tables) and converts them to standard TOML syntax in ``conf.toml``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:55
msgid "It detects standard Sphinx settings (such as ``project``, ``author``, ``extensions``, ``templates_path``, ``html_theme``, ``intersphinx_mapping``, and ``html_context``) and maps them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:58
msgid "It finds computed expressions (such as Python calls like ``version = get_version()`` or ``git_revision = subprocess.check_output(...)``). Guidedog does not run Python, so its migration report flags these values. We then give fixed values for them in ``conf.toml``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:63
msgid "We review the generated ``conf.toml`` and replace each flagged expression with a fixed value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:65
msgid "Step 2: The three-pass verification strategy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:68
msgid "Once ``conf.toml`` exists, we work through the migration in three passes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:70
msgid "Pass 1: Verify the document graph"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:73
msgid "We check that Guidedog finds all documents and builds the expected hierarchy:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:75
msgid "Verify that ``root_doc`` names our main entry point (usually ``index`` or ``contents``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:76
msgid "Confirm that ``source_suffix`` lists every extension we use (for example, ``[\".rst\", \".md\"]``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:77
msgid "Check that ``exclude_patterns`` excludes build folders, virtual environments, and temporary files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:78
msgid "Run a quick semantic check using the dummy builder:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:84
msgid "The dummy builder checks every document and link without writing HTML files. We fix each warning about a missing document or a malformed include."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:87
msgid "Pass 2: Verify references, domains, and custom objects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:90
msgid "Next, we verify that cross-references and domain directives resolve:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:92
msgid "**Standard domains:** Guidedog supports the standard Python, C, C++, and JavaScript domains, with their roles such as ``:py:func:``, ``:c:type:``, and ``:cpp:class:``. It adds ``odin`` and ``rust`` domains of its own (see :doc:`../topics/domains`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:95
msgid "**Intersphinx links:** If our Sphinx project linked to external documentation through Intersphinx, we keep our ``[intersphinx_mapping]`` in ``conf.toml``. Guidedog fetches and parses standard ``objects.inv`` files itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:98
msgid "**Declarative custom object types:** In Sphinx, projects often wrote small Python extensions that call ``app.add_object_type()`` to create custom directives and roles (such as ``.. confval::`` or ``.. setting::``). In Guidedog, we declare these in ``conf.toml`` under ``[[object_types]]``, without code. See :doc:`../object-types`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:103
msgid "Pass 3: Verify presentation and templates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:106
msgid "Finally, we check how the output looks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:108
msgid "**HTML website:** Run ``guidedog build html path/to/docs -W`` and inspect the generated pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:109
msgid "**Jinja templates:** Guidedog's native Jinja engine supports block inheritance:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:118
msgid "**PDF books:** Build a PDF book with ``guidedog build pdf path/to/docs -W``. Guidedog typesets the book with Typst and ``_templates/book.typ``. It gives vector math, proper hyphenation, and running headers without a LaTeX installation."
msgstr ""

